      "note": "Named 2026-08-31 by elimination, not by a sighting. Between S Burlington (542005, pinned the same day by four operator sightings) and S Vernon (549005) the archive contains exactly ONE well-received pair of 24-bit control points - this and 546005 - and the operator siding list has exactly one siding in that stretch, Midway MP 80.1-82.3. The pair also works its switches together: 19 of 21 reverse windows coupled. Knockdown timing anchored on 542005=72.8 independently gives MP 79.7. The 2026-08-09 operator series (MOVEMENT-20260809 sec 5, NB#1) interpolates this ID to MP 88.4 instead; that is rejected because 88-89 falls inside the Vernon siding, whose ends are 549005/549505 - which is the lagged-relay explanation that document's own sec 6.2 offered for the same conflict."
    },
