      "note": "2sw+4sig CP on the Waukesha Sub between Allenton (north) and N Ackerville (south), with two WAMX connections. Serialized field roles, 24 bits fully consumed: sw1[0:2] sw2[2:4] S1N[4:9] S1R[9:14] N2N[14:19] N2R[19:24]. SW1 is the west/north switch (reverse route to WAMX-Horicon), SW2 the east/south switch (reverse route to WAMX-Milwaukee). S1* is the north-facing pair governing southbound moves, N2* the south-facing pair governing northbound; the N head of each pair reads with its switch Normal, the R head with it Reverse. Layout established 2026-08-26 over 3830 frames (rpi5-Util capture wiu_20260825-185319): the 1sw/3sig CP layout yields 0% in-vocabulary aspects here, this one 100%; all five switch 'I' reads sit between an N frame and an R frame. Operator ground truth the same day - a northbound had N2N Clear 12:59:32-13:05:24; S1R (WAMX-Horicon) showed Red over Green 13:10:08-13:25:08, its only non-STOP interval in the whole capture, with both switches Reverse; S1N held Yellow over Green 19:00:16-19:57:28. Head names and geography from the operator's track diagram. Was an auto-generated 3-switch stub before this."
    },
